<%page args="profile_src"/>
## What the installer calls itself, and which Anaconda profile it uses.
##
## pixel-blue.conf inherits fedora-silverblue, which is what keeps the
## installation summary to the Silverblue set of spokes and its stylesheet, and
## what makes automatic partitioning match a bootc system (see the file itself
## for why the /var subvolume had to go).
##
## The two os-release keys are what select that profile: Anaconda matches
## /etc/os-release against /etc/anaconda/profile.d/*.conf, and
## variant_id=pixel-blue is a value no upstream profile claims. Appending wins
## over the Silverblue release package's own VARIANT_ID because os-release
## parsers take the last assignment.
##
## The product name and version on the window and in the buildstamp come from
## lorax's --product/--version/--isfinal, not from here.
runcmd mkdir -p ${root}/etc/anaconda/profile.d
runcmd cp -a ${profile_src}/pixel-blue.conf ${root}/etc/anaconda/profile.d/pixel-blue.conf
append usr/lib/os-release "VARIANT=\"Pixel Blue\""
append usr/lib/os-release "VARIANT_ID=pixel-blue"
